---
import ButtonLink from '../components/ButtonLink.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout description="Schep Capital tests whether daily price and volume data can support a long/short strategy with better risk-adjusted returns than the market and a maximum drawdown below 10%.">
  <header class="max-w-3xl py-4 sm:py-8 lg:py-12">
    <p class="eyebrow">Systematic trading research</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl text-balance sm:mt-3 sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.032em] text-ink">
      Can daily price and volume data deliver <span class="bg-linear-to-r from-accent-text to-secondary-text bg-clip-text text-transparent">better risk-adjusted returns</span> than the market?
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      I’m Reinier Schep. At Schep Capital, I use daily price and volume data to rank assets, decide
      how far to lean long or short, and size positions based on risk. I test how closely the
      portfolio should follow those target weights once trading costs are taken into account.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      My goal is steady returns, a higher Sortino ratio than a broad market benchmark, and a
      maximum drawdown below 10%. I test the strategy on unseen data and evaluate its performance
      after trading costs.
    </p>
    <ButtonLink href="/about/" variant="primary" class="mt-5">Read the research approach</ButtonLink>
  </header>
</Layout>
